<Base title="Support — Trypup" description="Need help with the Trypup app? Email us at support@trypup.life." lang="en" alt="/podpora/" pageKey="support">
  <section class="section wrap prose">
    <h1>Support</h1>
    <p class="meta">Have a question or something not working? Reach out — we're happy to help.</p>

    <p>Need help with the app, ran into a bug, or not sure how to care for your dog in Trypup? Drop us a line.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Support:</strong> <a href="mailto:support@trypup.life">support@trypup.life</a></li>
    </ul>
    <p>To help us route you faster, please include your <strong>phone model</strong>, <strong>OS</strong> (iOS / Android) and <strong>app version</strong> (found at the bottom of Settings) in your email.</p>

    <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>

    <h3>How does Trypup work?</h3>
    <p>Trypup does two things. <strong>Dog on trial:</strong> you pick a breed, name your dog and care for it for 30 days like the real thing — walks, feeding, training, vet. <strong>Dog at home:</strong> for your real dog — a dog passport, a diary, a care plan with reminders and first aid. You'll find more in the <a href="/en/#how-it-works">How it works</a> and <a href="/en/#dog-at-home">Dog at home</a> sections of the home page, or on the <a href="/en/about/">About</a> page. <a href="/en/#how-it-works">How it works</a> and <a href="/en/#dog-at-home">Dog at home</a>, or on the <a href="/en/about/">About</a> page.</p>

    <h3>How do I switch between Dog on trial and Dog at home?</h3>
    <p>In Settings, under “How you use Trypup”. Your virtual dog waits in the meantime, with its time paused; only a dog in shared care keeps going. An ongoing 30-day challenge ends as “The dog came home early”, with no evaluation. Dog at home has been in the app since version 2.0. If you don't see it yet, update the app; the new version is rolling out to everyone gradually.</p>

    <h3>Reminders aren't arriving. What can I do?</h3>
    <p>Check that Trypup is allowed to send notifications on your phone. Some Android phones put background apps to sleep to save battery, so turn off battery saving for Trypup in your battery settings. In the app's Settings, make sure reminders are turned on; for a dog in Dog at home mode you can also set the reminder time there. The care plan only reminds you of items you have confirmed.</p>

    <h3>How do I delete a dog in Dog at home mode?</h3>
    <p>Open the dog's details and choose <strong>Delete dog</strong>. If your dog is no longer with you, you can move them to the archive instead of deleting them.</p>

    <h3>How do I delete my account and data?</h3>
    <p>Right in the app: <strong>Profile → Account → Delete account</strong>. This deletes your account and the cloud backup, including the backup of your dogs from Dog at home mode. Dog at home data stored on your phone stays, though; you can delete it in <strong>Settings → Dog data</strong>. If you've already uninstalled the app, email support and we'll delete your data. Details: <a href="/en/delete-account/">Delete account</a>.</p>

    <h3>Subscriptions and payments</h3>
    <p>Your subscription (Premium) is managed by the App Store or Google Play — you can cancel it there anytime. Your dogs' data in Dog at home mode doesn't get locked after Premium ends. For anything else about payments, contact support.</p>

    <h3>What about my privacy?</h3>
    <p>The app works without an account and we process data only as needed. See our <a href="/en/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> for details.</p>

    <p>Didn't find your answer? <a href="mailto:support@trypup.life">Email us at support@trypup.life</a> — we're here for you.</p>
